e1c1c212-8f92-4822-b02c-fbcee922698d-0
00:49:20.720 --> 00:49:23.311
So whereas major depressive disorder is a
prevalent,

e1c1c212-8f92-4822-b02c-fbcee922698d-1
00:49:23.311 --> 00:49:26.488
recurrent and potentially life
threatening psychiatric condition

e1c1c212-8f92-4822-b02c-fbcee922698d-2
00:49:26.488 --> 00:49:28.982
associated with substantial functional
impairment,

e1c1c212-8f92-4822-b02c-fbcee922698d-3
00:49:28.982 --> 00:49:32.893
diminished quality of life and elevated
risk of suicide and remains the leading

e1c1c212-8f92-4822-b02c-fbcee922698d-4
00:49:32.893 --> 00:49:34.360
cause of disability worldwide.

b7d48d8f-aee4-4efb-b76c-92dc4ac952b7-0
00:49:34.760 --> 00:49:38.682
And whereas standard treatments for MDD
include antidepressant pharmacotherapy

b7d48d8f-aee4-4efb-b76c-92dc4ac952b7-1
00:49:38.682 --> 00:49:42.604
and psychotherapy are limited by delayed
onset of action in complete response,

b7d48d8f-aee4-4efb-b76c-92dc4ac952b7-2
00:49:42.604 --> 00:49:45.434
adverse effects,
and high rates of treatment resistance,

b7d48d8f-aee4-4efb-b76c-92dc4ac952b7-3
00:49:45.434 --> 00:49:48.761
leaving a significant proportion of
individuals with persistent or

b7d48d8f-aee4-4efb-b76c-92dc4ac952b7-4
00:49:48.761 --> 00:49:50.400
debilitating depressive symptoms.

27ff9c0f-3bf2-4c73-9576-81061b53ac80-0
00:49:50.400 --> 00:49:53.604
And whereas high quality randomized
clinical trials demonstrate that

27ff9c0f-3bf2-4c73-9576-81061b53ac80-1
00:49:53.604 --> 00:49:56.716
psilocybin assisted therapy produces
rapid, clinically meaningful,

27ff9c0f-3bf2-4c73-9576-81061b53ac80-2
00:49:56.716 --> 00:50:00.199
and sustained reductions in depressive
symptoms when administered within a

27ff9c0f-3bf2-4c73-9576-81061b53ac80-3
00:50:00.199 --> 00:50:03.682
structured therapeutic setting that
includes psychological preparation and

27ff9c0f-3bf2-4c73-9576-81061b53ac80-4
00:50:03.682 --> 00:50:04.240
integration.

1abb2338-b8ea-417c-98ea-eadb94dab5e0-0
00:50:04.440 --> 00:50:07.918
And whereas in a multi site, double-blind,
active, placebo-controlled,

1abb2338-b8ea-417c-98ea-eadb94dab5e0-1
00:50:07.918 --> 00:50:11.593
phase two randomized clinical trial
involving adults with major depressive

1abb2338-b8ea-417c-98ea-eadb94dab5e0-2
00:50:11.593 --> 00:50:14.092
disorder,
a single 25 milligram dose of psilocybin

1abb2338-b8ea-417c-98ea-eadb94dab5e0-3
00:50:14.092 --> 00:50:17.571
was associated with a large and
statistically significant reduction in

1abb2338-b8ea-417c-98ea-eadb94dab5e0-4
00:50:17.571 --> 00:50:21.343
the Montgomery Asperger Depression Rating
Scale scores compared with niacin,

1abb2338-b8ea-417c-98ea-eadb94dab5e0-5
00:50:21.343 --> 00:50:25.165
with antidepressant effects evident by
day 8 and sustained through six weeks,

1abb2338-b8ea-417c-98ea-eadb94dab5e0-6
00:50:25.165 --> 00:50:29.036
accompanied by significant improvement in
functional disability and no serious

1abb2338-b8ea-417c-98ea-eadb94dab5e0-7
00:50:29.036 --> 00:50:30.800
treatment emergence adverse effects.

4bad4705-2ebf-48d6-ac32-87dd9dd2d6f1-0
00:50:31.400 --> 00:50:33.736
WHEREAS,
these findings are consistent with an

4bad4705-2ebf-48d6-ac32-87dd9dd2d6f1-1
00:50:33.736 --> 00:50:37.564
earlier randomized clinical or earlier
randomized controlled evidence from a

4bad4705-2ebf-48d6-ac32-87dd9dd2d6f1-2
00:50:37.564 --> 00:50:40.895
trial conducted at John Hopkins
University in which two psilocybin

4bad4705-2ebf-48d6-ac32-87dd9dd2d6f1-3
00:50:40.895 --> 00:50:44.077
sessions combined with supportive
psychotherapy produced large,

4bad4705-2ebf-48d6-ac32-87dd9dd2d6f1-4
00:50:44.077 --> 00:50:46.562
very large effect sizes,
rapid symptom reduction,

4bad4705-2ebf-48d6-ac32-87dd9dd2d6f1-5
00:50:46.562 --> 00:50:50.390
and high rates of clinical responses and
remission at one month follow up in

4bad4705-2ebf-48d6-ac32-87dd9dd2d6f1-6
00:50:50.390 --> 00:50:52.280
adults with major depressive disorder.

03ebf985-82b5-4481-ac13-cb25e6b1886c-0
00:50:52.920 --> 00:50:57.217
And whereas converging pharmacological
and translational evidence indicates that

03ebf985-82b5-4481-ac13-cb25e6b1886c-1
00:50:57.217 --> 00:51:01.196
psilocybin acts as a rapid acting
antidepressant through serotonergic 5 HT

03ebf985-82b5-4481-ac13-cb25e6b1886c-2
00:51:01.196 --> 00:51:05.069
2A receptor agonism and downstream
neuroplastic mechanisms including the

03ebf985-82b5-4481-ac13-cb25e6b1886c-3
00:51:05.069 --> 00:51:08.889
modulation of glutaminergic signaling,
synaptogenesis and brain derived

03ebf985-82b5-4481-ac13-cb25e6b1886c-4
00:51:08.889 --> 00:51:10.800
neurotropic factor related pathways.

65f1069e-cd4b-498d-bd7e-5b378b1259d7-0
00:51:10.800 --> 00:51:13.868
Providing a biologically plausible
explanation for the rapid onset and

65f1069e-cd4b-498d-bd7e-5b378b1259d7-1
00:51:13.868 --> 00:51:16.720
durability of antidepressant effects
observed in clinical trials.

155deb66-2d83-4c2a-8d41-9068d89b8e23-0
00:51:17.240 --> 00:51:20.114
And whereas the magnitude,
rapid onset and durability of

155deb66-2d83-4c2a-8d41-9068d89b8e23-1
00:51:20.114 --> 00:51:23.795
antidepressant effects observed with
psilocybin assisted therapy compare

155deb66-2d83-4c2a-8d41-9068d89b8e23-2
00:51:23.795 --> 00:51:26.720
favorably to existing pharmacological
treatments for MDD.

1f2ac49a-4869-4693-b5da-75b49eb03a32-0
00:51:27.160 --> 00:51:29.234
Therefore,
the committee finds that the current body

1f2ac49a-4869-4693-b5da-75b49eb03a32-1
00:51:29.234 --> 00:51:31.152
of clinical,
systematic and mechanistic evidence

1f2ac49a-4869-4693-b5da-75b49eb03a32-2
00:51:31.152 --> 00:51:33.814
supports the inclusion of major
depressive disorder as a qualifying

1f2ac49a-4869-4693-b5da-75b49eb03a32-3
00:51:33.814 --> 00:51:36.320
condition within a regulated evidence
based psilocybin program.

